#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-merge-file(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:7
msgid "git-merge-file - Run a three-way file merge"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:15
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t'git merge-file' [-L <current-name> [-L <base-name> [-L <other-name>]]]\n"
"\t\t[--ours|--theirs|--union] [-p|--stdout] [-q|--quiet] "
"[--marker-size=<n>]\n"
"\t\t[--[no-]diff3] [--object-id] <current> <base> <other>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:26
msgid ""
"Given three files `<current>`, `<base>` and `<other>`, 'git merge-file' "
"incorporates all changes that lead from `<base>` to `<other>` into "
"`<current>`. The result ordinarily goes into `<current>`. 'git merge-file' "
"is useful for combining separate changes to an original. Suppose `<base>` is "
"the original, and both `<current>` and `<other>` are modifications of "
"`<base>`, then 'git merge-file' combines both changes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:31
msgid ""
"A conflict occurs if both `<current>` and `<other>` have changes in a common "
"segment of lines. If a conflict is found, 'git merge-file' normally outputs "
"a warning and brackets the conflict with lines containing <<<<<<< and "
">>>>>>> markers. A typical conflict will look like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:37
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t<<<<<<< A\n"
"\tlines in file A\n"
"\t=======\n"
"\tlines in file B\n"
"\t>>>>>>> B\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:43
msgid ""
"If there are conflicts, the user should edit the result and delete one of "
"the alternatives.  When `--ours`, `--theirs`, or `--union` option is in "
"effect, however, these conflicts are resolved favouring lines from "
"`<current>`, lines from `<other>`, or lines from both respectively.  The "
"length of the conflict markers can be given with the `--marker-size` option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:47
msgid ""
"If `--object-id` is specified, exactly the same behavior occurs, except that "
"instead of specifying what to merge as files, it is specified as a list of "
"object IDs referring to blobs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:51
msgid ""
"The exit value of this program is negative on error, and the number of "
"conflicts otherwise (truncated to 127 if there are more than that many "
"conflicts). If the merge was clean, the exit value is 0."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:55
msgid ""
"'git merge-file' is designed to be a minimal clone of RCS 'merge'; that is, "
"it implements all of RCS 'merge''s functionality which is needed by "
"linkgit:git[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:58
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:60
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--object-id`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:63
msgid ""
"Specify the contents to merge as blobs in the current repository instead of "
"files.  In this case, the operation must take place within a valid "
"repository."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:67
msgid ""
"If the `-p` option is specified, the merged file (including conflicts, if "
"any)  goes to standard output as normal; otherwise, the merged file is "
"written to the object store and the object ID of its blob is written to "
"standard output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:68
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-L <label>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:75
msgid ""
"This option may be given up to three times, and specifies labels to be used "
"in place of the corresponding file names in conflict reports. That is, `git "
"merge-file -L x -L y -L z a b c` generates output that looks like it came "
"from files x, y and z instead of from files a, b and c."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:76
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-p`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:79
msgid "Send results to standard output instead of overwriting `<current>`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:80
#, no-wrap
msgid "`-q`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:82
msgid "Quiet; do not warn about conflicts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:83
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--diff3`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:85
msgid "Show conflicts in \"diff3\" style."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:86
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--zdiff3`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:88
msgid "Show conflicts in \"zdiff3\" style."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:89
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--ours`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:90
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--theirs`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:91
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--union`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:94
msgid ""
"Instead of leaving conflicts in the file, resolve conflicts favouring our "
"(or their or both) side of the lines."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:95
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--diff-algorithm={patience|minimal|histogram|myers}`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:101
msgid ""
"Use a different diff algorithm while merging. The current default is "
"\"myers\", but selecting more recent algorithm such as \"histogram\" can "
"help avoid mismerges that occur due to unimportant matching lines (such as "
"braces from distinct functions). See also linkgit:git-diff[1] "
"`--diff-algorithm`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:103
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXAMPLES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:105
#, no-wrap
msgid "`git merge-file README.my README README.upstream`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:109
msgid ""
"combines the changes of README.my and README.upstream since README, tries to "
"merge them and writes the result into README.my."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:110
#, no-wrap
msgid "`git merge-file -L a -L b -L c tmp/a123 tmp/b234 tmp/c345`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:114
msgid ""
"merges tmp/a123 and tmp/c345 with the base tmp/b234, but uses labels `a` and "
"`c` instead of `tmp/a123` and `tmp/c345`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:115
#, no-wrap
msgid "`git merge-file -p --object-id abc1234 def567 890abcd`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-merge-file.adoc:119
msgid ""
"combines the changes of the blob abc1234 and 890abcd since def567, tries to "
"merge them and writes the result to standard output"
msgstr ""

